+4.1 For any feasible $v$ with $\|v-u^*\|_2\le\sigma$, [F2] and [F3] bound the absolute difference of the state running terms by $\|Q\|_\infty E\sqrt T C_s\sigma$, the terminal terms by $\|P\|M_T C_s\sigma$, and the control terms by $M\sqrt T M_c\sigma$. Hence $J(v)-J(u^*)\le C_J\sigma$. Under [A1] the cell-average lemma gives strong recovery for the control-only case. If $u^*$ is $L_u$-Lipschitz, for each $t$ in a cell its distance from the cell average is at most $L_uh_N$, so $\|P_Nu^*-u^*\|_2\le\sqrt T L_uh_N$. Substitution gives the stated $\rho_N$ rate and completes the sufficient-estimate branch. [A1, F1, F2, F3, given, algebra] ∎
 
